## Skills Protocol

Prefer firing a skill over improvising its job. If work looks like something a skill covers (a consistency check, a verification pass, a design review), invoke that skill. The user's phrasing is often the trigger — *"run a consistency check"*, *"brainstorm this"*, *"code review"* name skills, not generic verbs.

### The 8 auto-fire skills

The studio fires these automatically when their trigger matches — no permission ask, just a brief announcement:

| Skill | Fires when… |
|---|---|
| `using-superpowers` | Every chat starts. |
| `brainstorming` | Creative work begins — a new feature, mechanic, UI, or behaviour change. |
| `test-driven-development` | Implementation code is about to be written. |
| `systematic-debugging` | A bug / hang / crash / wrong-output report arrives. Evidence-gathering comes before fix attempts. |
| `verification-before-completion` | A "done / fixed / passing" claim, commit, or PR is coming up. Run the verification commands; cite the output. |
| `godot-engine` | Engine files are being edited (scripts, scenes, resources, shaders) or specced. (bundled; anthropic-skills plugin = optional upgrade) <!-- Non-Godot project: swap this row for the matching engine-pack skill --> |
| `session-close` | The session is ending ("wrap up", "we're done"), or 5+ commits have landed without a sync. |
| `writing-skills` | Any `SKILL.md` file is about to be created or edited. |

