## Project conventions

### Spec / Plan / ADR paths

| Skill | Writes to | Naming | Lifecycle |
|---|---|---|---|
| `brainstorming` | `docs/specs/` | `YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md` | 🚧 IN PROGRESS → ✅ FINAL → 🗄️ ARCHIVED to `docs/z-old/specs/` |
| `writing-plans` | `docs/plans/` | `YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-plan.md` | 🚧 ACTIVE → ✅ SHIPPED → 🗄️ ARCHIVED to `docs/z-old/plans/` |
| `architecture-decision` | `docs/adr/` | `NNN-<slug>.md` | Permanent. Use `docs/adr/TEMPLATE.md`. Batch 2–3 decisions per ADR. |

Every spec carries a `## Expected outcomes at ship` section near the top — what the designer can do/edit/test once it ships.

### State tracking

`data/_schemas/system_registry.json` is the single source of truth for "is it built?". Update it whenever a chat adds or changes a system, tool, or data category. Trust the registry over any prose doc if they disagree.

### Numbers live in data, not docs

Tunable values (formulas, stat tables, rarity bands, curves) live in editable data files — never hardcoded in a doc or in code. A doc points at the data file and names the tool/editor that edits it. Changing a number = editing data, not editing prose.

